  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Connecticut has recorded $212M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state logged 843 awards with an average award size of $252K, and obligations are down 99.2% year over year. Historical obligations show large annual swings: FY22 totaled $22.6B, FY23 totaled $26.5B, FY24 totaled $20.4B, FY25 totaled $35.4B, and FY26 totaled $27.6B. The Department of Homeland Security leads buying in FY2027 to date with $168M in obligations. WHITING-TURNER CONTRACTING COMPANY, THE is the largest vendor with $155M in obligations. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations with $160M. Other notable agencies include the Department of Veterans Affairs with $23.9M and the Department of Labor with $7.5M. Other notable vendors include CONTINUUM OF CARE INC with $6.6M and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $6M. Other industries receiving material obligations include Other Technical and Trade Schools with $7.5M and Residential Mental Health and Substance Abuse Facilities with $6.6M.",
